    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Owen Reilly are delighted to present No. 1 William Beckett House, a stunning two-bedroom apartment ideally located just off Lower Baggot Street. Set within a modern, highly sought-after development in Dublin’s central business district, this superb property is within a short stroll of St. Stephen’s Green and the city’s principal commercial and cultural hubs.\r\n\r\nSituated on the ground floor and extending to approximately 78 sq. m., the apartment offers bright, spacious, and well-appointed accommodation, finished to a high specification throughout. The layout comprises an inviting entrance hall, a generous living/dining room, two double bedrooms, a stylish kitchen, a luxurious shower room, and a main bathroom. Residents also benefit from access to a wonderful communal courtyard garden.\r\n\r\nThe location is truly exceptional, positioned just moments from the Grand Canal and the beautifully rejuvenated Wilton Park, offering an attractive outdoor amenity. The property is also within walking distance of major employers including LinkedIn, Amazon, Google, and Meta, making it an ideal choice for .\r\n\r\nWith a prestigious address and strong investment potential, this outstanding apartment will appeal to both owner-occupiers and investors alike.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended.\r\n\r\nMore about the location...\r\n\r\nPositioned just off Lower Baggot Street—one of Dublin’s premier city centre addresses—the area boasts an array of cafés, bars, and restaurants, alongside a rich selection of cultural landmarks, art galleries, and theatres. St Stephen’s Green, Grafton Street, Trinity College, and the Royal College of Surgeons are all within a short walking distance.\r\n\r\nThe Grand Canal and the beautifully rejuvenated Wilton Park are just moments away, providing an attractive outdoor amenity. The property is also ideally located for , with major employers such as LinkedIn, Amazon, Google, and Meta nearby. Excellent transport links further enhance the location, with regular bus services and the DART at Pearse Street close at hand."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall (3.62m x 1.13m)\r\nWelcoming entrance hall featuring wood-effect flooring and a hot press providing additional storage.\r\n\r\nLiving Room / Dining Room (6.5m x 3.4m)\r\nBright and spacious reception room with wood-effect flooring, a feature panelled wall, and recessed spot lighting. A large floor-to-ceiling window and door open onto the terrace.\r\n\r\nKitchen (3m x 2.8m)\r\nStylish kitchen fitted with a range of built-in wall and floor units, along with integrated appliances including an electric hob, oven, stainless steel extractor fan, fridge/freezer, dishwasher, and washing machine. Finished with tiled flooring, a splashback, and recessed spot lighting.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1 (3.3m x 2.7m and 2.6m x 1m)\r\nDouble bedroom with built in wardrobes and wood effect flooring.\r\n\r\nEn-suite Shower Room (1.96m x 1.9m)\r\nFully tiled and finished with ceramic marble-effect tiles. Comprises a step-in shower enclosure, WHB, WC, and heated towel rail.\r\n\r\nBathroom (2.3m x 1.76m)\r\nElegantly appointed, fully tiled bathroom featuring a wash hand basin set within a vanity unit, a large recessed mirror, concealed cistern WC, and a bath with overhead shower. Includes a heated towel rail and recessed spot lighting.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (2.3m x 2.3m and 1.16m x 1.7m)\r\nDouble bedroom with built in wardrobes.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\n\r\nTerrace (1.4m x 3.1m)"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Prime location just off Lower Baggot Street in the heart of Georgian Dublin.\r\nSpacious two-bedroom ground floor apartment extending to approx. 78 sq. m.\r\nBright and well-appointed accommodation with high-spec finish.\r\nStylish kitchen with separate living/dining area.\r\nTerrace set off the living room.\r\nTwo bathrooms, including a luxurious shower room.\r\nAccess to a wonderful communal courtyard garden.\r\nWithin walking distance of St. Stephen’s Green, Grand Canal, and major employers such as LinkedIn, Google, and Meta.\r\nService charge €2,400 p.a.\r\nElectric heating.\r\nSecure access."
      },
      {
